For simple cases, I use useEffect with fetch or axios. But on larger apps, I use TanStack Query because it handles so much more automatically — fetching, caching, refetching, error handling — all with minimal code.
Instead of writing useEffect + useState + loading state + error state yourself, you just call:
const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['patients'],
  queryFn: () => fetch('/api/patients').then(r => r.json()),
  staleTime: 30000 // refetch after 30 seconds
});
It also does background refetching — if you navigate away and come back, it automatically re-fetches stale data. On ZEOS dashboards, this was really useful for keeping data fresh.

